 "wikitext": "{{Short description|none}}\n{{Use Philippine English|date=September 2022}}\n{{Use mdy dates|date=September 2022}}\n[[File:Legislative_Districts_of_Sorsogon.png|right|400x400px]]\n{{Politics of the Philippines}}\nThe '''legislative districts of Sorsogon''' are the representations of the [[Provinces of the Philippines|province]] of [[Sorsogon]] in the [[List of legislatures of the Philippines|various national legislatures]] of the [[Philippines]]. The province is currently represented in the [[House of Representatives of the Philippines|lower house]] of the [[Congress of the Philippines]] through its [[#1st District|first]] and [[#2nd District|second]] congressional districts.\n\n== History ==\n[[Sorsogon]] initially comprised a [[#At-Large (defunct)|single district]] to the [[Malolos Congress]] from 1898 to 1899. It was later divided into two [[House of Representatives of the Philippines#District representation|congressional districts]] since 1907, which included [[Masbate]] until it was given its [[Legislative districts of Masbate|own representation]] in 1922. From 1978 to 1984, it was part of the representation of [[Interim Batasang Pambansa|Region V]] in the [[Interim Batasang Pambansa]], and it elected two assemblymen at-large in the [[Regular Batasang Pambansa]] from 1984 to 1986.\n\n== Current districts ==\n{| class=\"wikitable sortable\" style=\"margin: 1em auto; font-size:100%; line-height:20px; text-align:center\"\n|+Legislative districts and representatives of [[Sorsogon]]\n!District\n! colspan=\"3\" |Current Representative\n!Party\n!Constituent [[Local government in the Philippines|LGUs]]\n!Population (2020)\n!Area\n!Map\n|-\n![[Sorsogon's 1st congressional district|1st]]\n| style=\"background:{{party color|Nationalist People's Coalition}};\" |\n|{{CSS image crop|Image=Rep. Marie Bernadette Escudero (20th Congress).jpg|bSize = 120|cWidth = 120|cheight = 120|oTop = 0|oLeft = 0}}\n| style=\"text-align:left;\" |'''[[Dette Escudero|Marie Bernadette  Escudero]]'''<br><small>(since [[19th Congress of the Philippines|2022]])</small><br><small>[[Sorsogon City]]</small>\n|[[Nationalist People's Coalition|NPC]]\n|{{Collapsible list|[[Casiguran, Sorsogon|Casiguran]]|[[Castilla, Sorsogon|Castilla]]|[[Donsol, Sorsogon|Donsol]]|[[Magallanes, Sorsogon|Magallanes]]|[[Pilar, Sorsogon|Pilar]]|[[Sorsogon City]]\n}}\n|441,959<ref name=\"psa\">{{cite web|url=https://psa.gov.ph/sites/default/files/attachments/ird/specialrelease/2_Table%201%20Population%20of%20Legislative%20Districts%20by%20Province%20and%20Selected%20HUC_Component%20City%20Web%20Final-signed.pdf |title=TABLE 1. Population of legislative districts by Region, Province, and selected Highly Urbanized/Component City : 2020 |publisher=[[Philippine Statistics Authority]] |accessdate=June 17, 2022}}</ref>\n|1,103.73&nbsp;km<sup>2</sup>\n| [[File:First District in Sorsogon.svg|200px]]\n|-\n![[Sorsogon's 2nd congressional district|2nd]]\n| style=\"background:{{party color|Nationalist People's Coalition}};\" |\n| {{CSS image crop|Image=Rep. Wowo Fortes (20th Congress).jpg|bSize = 120|cWidth = 120|cheight = 120|oTop = 0|oLeft = 0}}\n| style=\"text-align:left;\" |'''[[Wowo Fortes|Manuel Fortes, Jr.]]'''<br><small>(since [[19th Congress of the Philippines|2022]])</small><br><small>[[Barcelona, Sorsogon|Barcelona]]</small>\n|[[Nationalist People's Coalition|NPC]]\n|{{Collapsible list|[[Barcelona, Sorsogon|Barcelona]]|[[Bulan, Sorsogon|Bulan]]|[[Bulusan, Sorsogon|Bulusan]]|[[Gubat]]|[[Irosin]]|[[Juban, Sorsogon|Juban]]|[[Matnog]]|[[Prieto Diaz]]|[[Santa Magdalena, Sorsogon|Santa Magdalena]]\n}}\n|386,696<ref name=\"psa\" />\n|1,015.28&nbsp;km<sup>2</sup>\n| [[File:Second District in Sorsogon.svg|200px]]\n|}\n\n<!--\n== [[Sorsogon's 1st congressional district|1st District]] ==\n[[File:First District in Sorsogon.svg|border|thumb|260x260px|Map of the first legislative district of Sorsogon]] This section is linked from [[1st National Assembly of the Philippines]] \n*'''[[Cities